    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="lede">
          The best gluten-free protein powder for most people is Garden of Life Sport Organic Plant-Based Protein, which brand and retailer listings describe as NSF Certified Gluten-Free, alongside NSF Certified for Sport and USDA Organic status, with about 30 g of protein per serving. Dymatize ISO100 is the best-known whey labeled gluten-free, OWYN Pro Elite works to an under-10 ppm standard for allergy-conscious households, and Naked Pea is the budget pick. A US gluten-free claim means under 20 ppm of gluten, but only third-party certification such as GFCO, at 10 ppm or less, adds outside testing, which matters most if you have celiac disease.
        </p>

        <QuickPicks products={PRODUCTS} />

        <div id="quick-comparison" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. Gluten-Free Protein Powders Compared
          </h2>

          <p>
            The answer first. These are the eight powders we rank, with protein per scoop, calories, sugar, price tier and gluten status. Price tier reflects cost per 25 g of protein at typical retail prices when we checked. The certification column separates third-party gluten-free certification from a brand's own gluten-free claim, because for someone with celiac disease that difference matters. Figures come from labels and brand listings at the time of writing and vary by flavor.
          </p>

