                  Whey itself contains no gluten, since it comes from milk. Flavored whey powders can still contain gluten through barley malt, cookie pieces or other additions, or through cross-contact during manufacturing. Look for a gluten-free claim or certification on the tub, especially if you have celiac disease, rather than assuming all whey is safe.
                </p>
