            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>What does certified gluten-free mean on protein powder?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  It means an independent organization has audited the manufacturing process and tests the product against its standard. GFCO, for example, certifies products at 10 ppm of gluten or less, half the FDA's 20 ppm limit for a gluten-free claim. A brand's own gluten-free claim must meet the FDA limit, but no outside testing is required.
                </p>
              </div>
