            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Is 20 ppm gluten safe for celiac disease?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  The FDA chose 20 ppm because research indicated most people with celiac disease tolerate that level, and it matches the international Codex standard. Some people are more sensitive and prefer products certified at 10 ppm or less. Your gastroenterologist or dietitian can advise how strict you need to be, based on your symptoms and test results.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

