                  Pea, rice, hemp, pumpkin and soy proteins contain no gluten, but they can be cross-contaminated during growing, milling or manufacturing, and some plant powders add oat or grain ingredients. A plant powder with a gluten-free certification, such as Garden of Life Sport per the brand, is safer for celiac disease than one without any gluten statement.
                </p>
