                  Usually, yes, for people avoiding gluten by preference, because the FDA requires a gluten-free claim to mean under 20 ppm. For celiac disease, a seal adds independent testing that the FDA does not require. A claim from a brand with a short ingredient list is a reasonable second choice; a product with no gluten statement is worth questioning.
